        "TextSection": {
            "TextSectionType": "Definition",
            "Contents": "A parasitic disease caused by protozoa of the genus <i>Leishmania</i> (>20 pathogenic species) transmitted by the bite of infected female phlebotomine sandflies. Three main syndromes are recognized: visceral (VL) cutaneous (CL; localized and diffuse forms) and mucocutaneous leishmaniasis. Post-kala-azar dermal leishmaniasis (PKDL) is a cutaneous sequela of VL. Most infections remain asymptomatic."
        },
